  "body": "Closes #1409\nClaim: mac/mac-mbp\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (mac/mac-mbp-w1409)\n\n### Problem\nNo icon uses the iOS 27 Icon Composer glass (layers, specular, translucency, system shadow).\n\n### Change\n- New pack « Liquid Glass » (`AppIconPack.glass`) with `glass-h` (H plein cadre), `glass-face-ring` (Face anneau), `glass-face-disc` (Face disque): `Icon-GLASS-H`, `Icon-GLASS-FACE-RING`, `Icon-GLASS-FACE-DISC` (`.icon` files), data-only `AppIconOption` cases.\n- The three names added to `ASSETCATALOG_COMPILER_ALTERNATE_APPICON_NAMES` in all 3 configurations of the app target that set it (Debug, Release, Beta).\n- Previews from `scripts/icon-previews.sh` (IconPreview image sets); ICONS.md §2 rows and CREDITS AlternativeIcons row. The assessment table stays on the issue. No existing icon touched.\n- Face parts split from `Icon-REDFACE.icon/Assets/foreground.svg`, same coordinates (ring and features copied verbatim). The disc (r=78) is the ring's outer edge (74.2 + 3.85). The red features keep stroke 7.7 (the prototype's 9 was not needed: legible at 58 px, checked).\n- Dark/Clear/Tinted: the system derives them from the layers (as for `Icon-REDFACE`); the fill specializations (default, dark) are the REDFACE ones.\n\n### Tests\n- `theLiquidGlassIconsHaveTheirRawValueNameTitlePackAndNoWindow` (new); the pack-order expectations now include `.glass`. Existing icon tests pass, including `everyAlternateIconNameIsInTheBuiltInfoPlist`, `everyAlternateIconOfTheBuildHasAnOptionWithAPack` and the preview check.\n- `AppIconPackTests` and `AppIconSettingsModelTests` run on a fresh iOS 27.2 simulator (deleted after): TEST SUCCEEDED. `pre-commit run --all-files` passes.\n- SwiftLint checked by hand on the two Swift files: line_length (none over 140), file_length, type_body_length (219 code lines in the test struct), large_tuple (a struct, no tuple), trailing_comma, vertical_whitespace, identifier_name, modifier_order.\n\n### ICONS.md §5 checklist\n- [x] 1024 px renders in Default, Dark, ClearLight, ClearDark, TintedLight, TintedDark with ictool: all three read as glass; contact sheet kept locally (not committed)\n- [x] readable at 29 pt (58 px render): H, ring and disc faces legible\n- [x] not a dated icon; no legacy raw value involved\n- [x] original art derived from the existing H and face, CREDITS updated\n- [ ] Home Screen check on the Duo (light, dark, Clear, Tinted): to list on #893 for the next device review\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEAZJkg4akNJrTQb2i\n",
