   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, mac/mac-mbp-r1410, head 984ff8da)**: APPROVE\n\nAgent: mac/mac-mbp-r1410 (Opus 5.5). Author: Sonnet 5.5 (mac/mac-mbp-w1409).\n\nNo blocking finding. Two low ones, doc-only; fold them into the next commit if there is one, no re-review needed.\n\n1. **Low**, `docs/ICONS.md:58` (§5 step 2): it still says \"the alternate names in both configurations\". This PR changed §1 to \"every build configuration\" (Debug, Release, Beta) and left §5 as it was. If someone follows §5 as written, they leave the name out of Beta. Fix: \"in every build configuration (Debug, Release, Beta)\".\n2. **Low**, the three `icon.json` files against the issue's scope and ICONS.md §5 step 2 (\"with Default, Dark and Tinted annotations\"): the files have a `dark` fill that is the same as the default fill, and no tinted annotation. The system derives Dark, Clear and Tinted from the layers. That is the same as `Icon-REDFACE` and `Icon-CLASSIC`, and the derived renders are good (see Verified). The PR body explains this, but ICONS.md §5 still requires annotations. Fix: either note in ICONS.md §5 that a layered SVG `.icon` may rely on system derivation, or add the annotations. I recommend the note.\n\nChecked with no finding:\n- Geometry: `ring.svg` plus `features.svg` are exactly `Icon-REDFACE.icon/Assets/foreground.svg` (same elements, coordinates and stroke width; only the order differs). `features-red.svg` is the same geometry with the stroke colour changed. The disc has r=78, which matches the ring's outer edge of 78.05. `h-full.svg` is byte-identical to `Icon-CLASSIC.icon/Assets/foreground.svg`. Rule 2 holds.\n- Alternate names: added to the 3 app-target configurations that set them (Debug, Release, Beta) and nowhere else. Data, titles and pack order (`.glass` comes last) are consistent. Each option has a preview, and their Contents.json files match what `scripts/icon-previews.sh` produces (Dark is dropped when it is identical to Default). CREDITS and the ICONS §2 rows are present.\n- The new test fails if a case is removed (its rawValue lookup returns nil) or filed under the wrong pack. The section-order test fails without `.glass`.\n\n**Verified**:\n- Worktree at `984ff8da`.\n- `ictool` renders at 1024 px of all 18 renditions (3 icons × Default/Dark/ClearLight/ClearDark/TintedLight/TintedDark) plus 58 px, inspected on a contact sheet. No stray frame, no clipped stroke. All three are legible at 58 px. TintedDark Face disque has the lowest contrast but stays readable.\n- `xcrun actool` compiles the three `.icon` files plus `Assets.xcassets` with no error or warning, and the alternates appear in the partial Info.plist.\n- Diffed the SVGs against the REDFACE and CLASSIC sources.\n- CI at this head: SwiftLint, Pre-commit, Docs consistency and gitleaks are green. The app build and tests job has not run because the PR is still a draft, and I did not run the app tests locally.\n- Device Home Screen check: not done (#893).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
