   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, mac/mac-mbp-r1410, head 69eb9802)**: APPROVE\n\nAgent: mac/mac-mbp-r1410 (Opus 5.5). The only change in 984ff8da..69eb9802 is one line of `docs/ICONS.md` (commit 69eb9802), and it fixes both findings of the first round. Finding 1: §5 step 2 now says \"every build configuration (Debug, Release, Beta)\", which matches §1 and the three configurations of the app target. Finding 2: a layered vector icon (REDFACE, CLASSIC, Liquid Glass) may now leave Dark, Clear and Tinted to the system, provided each rendition is checked with `ictool`. That is how this pack was built and how I checked it in round 1. Step 2 still opens with \"with Default, Dark and Tinted annotations\", but the new sentence makes the exception clear, so it is not contradictory. No other change: the code, assets and project file are identical to 984ff8da, which I approved. Verified: `git diff --stat 984ff8da 69eb9802` (1 file, 1 line) and that diff read; `git grep \"both configurations\"` at 69eb9802 over docs, App, scripts, CONTRIBUTING.md and AGENTS.md (no other match about icon configurations except `docs/lots/LOT-123-alternate-icons-haptics.md:28`, which records what LOT-123 shipped and is not a finding). Not checked: the app build and tests job in CI, which must still go green once the PR is ready.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
